meta {
  name: 05 - Update Collection Item (CAUTION)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

put {
  url: {{base_url}}/collections/{{collection_id}}/items
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{craft_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "itemsToUpdate": [
      {
        "id": "{{test_item_id}}",
        "properties": {
          "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_PROPERTY_KEY": "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_VALUE"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  SUPERSEDED for the core "mark applied" flow: request 06 showed a
  collection item's `properties` are company-level aggregate counters
  (offres_postules, etc.), not a per-offer toggle - the actual per-offer
  state lives in nested task blocks, handled by request 09 instead
  (PUT /blocks, not this endpoint).

  Kept as a template in case you later want wm_automation to also
  increment these aggregate counters (e.g. offres_postules) alongside
  flipping the per-offer task block - not wired up, not needed yet.

  WRITE request - mutates a real tracker row if you do run it. Set
  `test_item_id` to a company id you're fine touching, and replace
  REPLACE_WITH_* with a real property key/value from request 03's schema
  first.
}
